  "comments": "The authorship of the work comes to be ascribed to the future Buddha Maitreya (ID:3747) in the Indian tradition from the 11th c. onward and in the Tibetan tradition. On earlier witnesses ascribing the authorship to S\u0101ramati or Sthiramati, see [BAQ9MH4T]: 20-27. No attribution of that work to Asa\u1e45ga (ID:3756) was located in Indian sources, but the colophon of the Tibetan translation by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab ascribes the verses to Maitreya and the prose commentary to Asa\u1e45ga ([BAQ9MH4T]: 27-28).\r\nThere are six Tibetan translations, only that by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab and Sajjana is currently extant ([BAQ9MH4T]: chap. 6).",
